    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n97197" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στρηνής</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ές</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>rough, harsh</i>, esp. of
			sounds: hence neut. as Adv., [
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὕδωρ] στρηνὲς περὶ στυφελῇ βρέμει
					ἀκτῇ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.R.
					2.323
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στρηνὲς φωνεῦσα [θάλασσα</span>] <i><span class="en">
				<u>AP</u>
				7.287
			</span></i> (Antip.); <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σάλπιγξ στρηνὲς
				φθεγξαμένη</span>
			<i>piercing</i>, ib.<i><span class="en">
				6.350
			</span></i> (<i><span class="en">
				Crin.
			</span></i>): cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στρηνός, στρηνύζω</span>.
			(Perh. connected with <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στερεός</span>, Lat.
				<i>strenuus.</i>)</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
